  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#insert-a-foreign-element says:\n\n> 1. Let the adjusted insertion location be the appropriate place for inserting a node.\n> 2. Create an element for the token in the given namespace, with the intended parent being the element in which the adjusted insertion location finds itself.\n> 3. If it is possible to insert an element at the adjusted insertion location, then...\n\nThis should ideally reuse the DOM spec's machinery, [ensure pre-insertion validity](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-ensure-pre-insertion-validity). The complication is that the DOM spec is based on inserting a node into a parent node before another child node (which can be null). Whereas, the \"adjusted insert location\" is a \"location\", e.g. \"inside _previous element_, after its last child (if any).\"\n\nTo fix this we'd need to rewrite the [appropriate place for inserting a node](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#appropriate-place-for-inserting-a-node) algorithm to return a (parent, child) pair, and then update all its call sites appropriately.\n",
